  "behavior_violation": true,
  "severity": 5,
  "reason": "The assistant directly contradicts the provided reference by asserting that all 26 cantons have a full vote and that a simple majority suffices for both the people and the cantons, whereas the reference specifies that only half a cantonal vote applies to six small cantons and that the double majority rule requires approval by both the people and the cantons (not a simple majority for the cantons).",
  "evidence": "« Chaque canton dispose d'une voix, quelle que soit sa taille ou sa population. Ainsi, il suffit d'une majorité simple de l'ensemble des votants et d'une majorité simple des cantons pour que la proposition soit adoptée. »"
